        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Game Title:</strong> <i>Shards of the Library</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Playtime:</strong> Approximately 1–2 hours (You can continue playing freely after finishing the main quests)</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >🧩 Gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Shards of the Library</i> is a story-driven simulation and puzzle game with farming elements and mysterious events that unfold within a strange library.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Players can:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore a small open-world village with seasonal changes and a day/night cycle</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Complete 90+ quests involving farming, cooking, potion crafting, and toolmaking</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Interact with 40+ unique NPCs and engage in systems like music performance, painting, and writing</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enter procedurally generated forests and caves</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Build relationships, discover secrets, and collect artifacts</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game also features fishing, monster encounters, item crafting (70+), farming crops (15+ types), skill learning (50+), and more.<br>Even after completing the main quests, players can continue enjoying daily farm life at their own pace.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >📖 Game Story</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One day, the protagonist receives a letter from their grandfather, asking them to take care of his farm while he goes on an unexpected journey.<br>After arriving and settling into a quiet rural life, the protagonist visits the town library—only to discover that something strange is happening through the books they borrow.<br>In a world where ordinary life and mystery are intertwined, players will gradually uncover hidden truths.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >🛠 Developer's Note</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game is a solo-developed project created as part of a graduation portfolio, using skills learned from CSE360 and CSE412 courses.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It was inspired by titles such as <i>Stardew Valley</i>, <i>Mabinogi</i>, and <i>Princess Maker</i>.<br>All systems listed above are already implemented and playable.<br>Future updates may include polish, bug fixes, and small expansions based on player feedback.<br>We appreciate your understanding as development continues during Early Access.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >🎥 Distribution &amp; Streaming Notice</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you share or stream this game, please include the game title or a Steam link in your video description.<br>Unauthorized redistribution is not supported, and we are not responsible for any issues caused by it.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Game Title:</strong> <i>Shards of the Library</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Playtime:</strong> Approximately 1–2 hours (You can continue playing freely after finishing the main quests)</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >🧩 Gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Shards of the Library</i> is a story-driven simulation and puzzle game with farming elements and mysterious events that unfold within a strange library.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Players can:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore a small open-world village with seasonal changes and a day/night cycle</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Complete 90+ quests involving farming, cooking, potion crafting, and toolmaking</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Interact with 40+ unique NPCs and engage in systems like music performance, painting, and writing</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enter procedurally generated forests and caves</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Build relationships, discover secrets, and collect artifacts</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game also features fishing, monster encounters, item crafting (70+), farming crops (15+ types), skill learning (50+), and more.<br>Even after completing the main quests, players can continue enjoying daily farm life at their own pace.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >📖 Game Story</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One day, the protagonist receives a letter from their grandfather, asking them to take care of his farm while he goes on an unexpected journey.<br>After arriving and settling into a quiet rural life, the protagonist visits the town library—only to discover that something strange is happening through the books they borrow.<br>In a world where ordinary life and mystery are intertwined, players will gradually uncover hidden truths.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >🛠 Developer's Note</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game is a solo-developed project created as part of a graduation portfolio, using skills learned from CSE360 and CSE412 courses.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It was inspired by titles such as <i>Stardew Valley</i>, <i>Mabinogi</i>, and <i>Princess Maker</i>.<br>All systems listed above are already implemented and playable.<br>Future updates may include polish, bug fixes, and small expansions based on player feedback.<br>We appreciate your understanding as development continues during Early Access.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >🎥 Distribution &amp; Streaming Notice</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you share or stream this game, please include the game title or a Steam link in your video description.<br>Unauthorized redistribution is not supported, and we are not responsible for any issues caused by it.</p>",
